ood value for money.\",\"categories\":[{\"label\":\"Bed Comfort\",\"score\":9.5},{\"label\":\"Service\",\"score\":9},{\"label\":\"Location\",\"score\":9},{\"label\":\"Room Size\",\"score\":8.5},{\"label\":\"Breakfast\",\"score\":7.5}],\"providers\":[{\"name\":\"Booking.com\",\"score\":8.3,\"reviews\":1612},{\"name\":\"Agoda.com\",\"score\":8.7,\"reviews\":60},{\"name\":\"HotelsCombined\",\"score\":8.7,\"reviews\":1}],\"mentions\":[\"spacious room\",\"friendly staff\",\"comfortable bed\",\"great location\",\"great breakfast\",\"free parking\",\"good value for money\",\"shower to small\",\"pod coffee machine\",\"clean and tidy\"],\"qa\":[{\"question\":\"What can I expect from the hotel\'s breakfast options?\",\"answer\":\"The hotel offers a free continental breakfast with a variety of options, although some guests have mentioned that they would appreciate a wider selection and a more buffet-style setup.\"},{\"question\":\"How are the hotel\'s beds described by guests?\",\"answer\":\"Guests have consistently praised the hotel\'s beds, describing them as exceptionally comfortable and spacious, ensuring a good night\'s sleep.\"},{\"question\":\"Is the hotel\'s cleanliness up to standard?\",\"answer\":\"While many guests have commended the hotel\'s cleanliness, some have mentioned specific areas that needed attention, such as the bathroom and the need for improved carpet cleaning.\"},{\"question\":\"What are the parking options at the hotel?\",\"answer\":\"The hotel offers free parking, which has been appreciated by many guests. However, a few guests have mentioned the need for additional parking spaces during peak times.\"},{\"question\":\"How would you describe the hotel\'s customer service?\",\"answer\":\"Guests have consistently praised the hotel\'s friendly and helpful staff, although a few have mentioned the need for improvements in addressing specific concerns and room maintenance.\"}],\"tips\":[{\"title\":\"Opt for a Room on the Ground Floor\",\"text\":\"Several guests recommended requesting a ground floor room for a quieter experience, as noise from upstairs rooms was mentioned in some reviews.\"},{\"title\":\"Consider Bringing Kitchen Utensils\",\"text\":\"Some guests noted a lack of kitchen utensils, so if you plan to cook, consider bringing your own utensils for convenience.\"},{\"title\":\"Check Breakfast Details\",\"text\":\"Some guests were surprised by the limited options of the continental breakfast, so it\'s advisable to inquire about the breakfast details before booking if it\'s an important factor for your stay.\"},{\"title\":\"Request Room Servicing\",\"text\":\"If you prefer regular room servicing, it\'s recommended to communicate this with the staff to ensure your preferences are met.\"},{\"title\":\"Be Mindful of Noise\",\"text\":\"Several guests mentioned noise from other guests, so being mindful of noise levels can contribute to a more peaceful environment for all guests.\"},{\"title\":\"Inquire About Renovations\",\"text\":\"If you\'re sensitive to construction-related disturbances, it\'s advisable to inquire about any ongoing or upcoming renovations at the hotel.\"},{\"title\":\"Consider Bringing Toiletries\",\"text\":\"Some guests mentioned a lack of certain toiletries, so consider bringing your own to ensure you have everything you need for your stay.\"},{\"title\":\"Verify Room Facilities\",\"text\":\"It\'s recommended to verify the availability of specific room facilities, such as a full-length mirror or kitchen equipment, to ensure they meet your expectations.\"},{\"title\":\"Check for Room Upgrades\",\"text\":\"Some guests received free room upgrades, so it may be worth inquiring about the possibility of an upgrade during your stay.\"},{\"title\":\"Plan for Parking\",\"text\":\"If you\'re arriving by car, it\'s advisable to plan for parking, especially if the hotel\'s parking spaces are limited.\"}],\"crawled_at\":\"2026-11-19 23:05:43\"}','0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL);
/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `hotels` ENABLE KEYS */;
UNLOCK TABLES;
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS `places`;
/*!40101 SET @saved_cs_client     = @@character_set_client */;
/*!50503 SET character_set_client = utf8mb4 */;
CREATE TABLE `places` (
  `id` int NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,
  `category_id` int DEFAULT NULL,
  `country_id` int DEFAULT NULL,
  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,
  `slug` varchar(255) CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_0900_ai_ci DEFAULT NULL,
  `address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,
  `image` varchar(255) CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_0900_ai_ci DEFAULT NULL,
  `content` text CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_0900_ai_ci,
  `rating` tinyint DEFAULT NULL,
  `is_featured` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',
  `crawler_href` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,
  `crawler_credit` varchar(500) DEFAULT NULL,
  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,
  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,
  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),
  UNIQUE KEY `uq_places_slug` (`slug`),
  KEY `fk_places_country` (`country_id`),
  CONSTRAINT `fk_places_country` FOREIGN KEY (`country_id`) REFERENCES `countries` (`id`) ON DELETE SET NULL
) ENGINE=InnoDB AUTO_INCREMENT=26 DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb4 COLLATE=utf8mb4_0900_ai_ci;
/*!40101 SET character_set_client = @saved_cs_client */;

LOCK TABLES `places` WRITE;
/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `places` DISABLE KEYS */;
INSERT INTO `places` VALUES (4,3,1,'Phu Quoc','phu-quoc','Phu Quoc, Vietnam','kayak_f5c9a78bb536a390fc2933890287591f.jpg','Which is the best area to stay in if I would like to be close to the airport?\nTo be just a short distance from Phu Quoc International Airport, try to stay in a hotel in the southern region of the island. The MyPlace Siena Garden Resort is a chic option that is just a 5min drive from the airport, while the Long Beach Resort Phu Quoc is a 4-star choice that is a 6min drive away.\n\nWhich is the best area for budget-conscious travellers to stay in?\nFor those who will be sticking to a budget during their travels, select lodging in the neighbourhood of Cửa Cạn, an area known for being particularly affordable. The Phu Quoc EcoLodge offers competitive prices and is located directly next to the water, while Chez Carole Beach Resort is charming yet affordable.\n\nWhere should I stay to be close to nightlife?\nIf you’re hoping to experience some of the city’s vibrant nightlife, search for hotels in Phu Quoc in the neighbourhood of Duong Dong, such as the Garden House Phu Quoc Resort or the Chen Sea Resort & Spa Phu Quoc. Duong Dong is known for being lively and having many bars, including the Lion Garden Beer Club, Itaca Resto Lounge, and Dinh Cau Night Market.\n\nWhat is a convenient area to stay in if I will be travelling to other islands?\nTo easily travel to nearby islands, select a hotel in the southern region of Phu Quoc, such as the JW Marriott Phu Quoc Emerald Bay Resort & Spa. This will put you just a short drive from the local ferry, which can take you to places like Lighthouse Islet and Roi Island.\n\nWhich freebies do KAYAK users look for when booking a hotel in Phu Quoc?\nKAYAK users look for a hotel in Phu Quoc with free breakfast. Hotels with free breakfast in Phu Quoc include The Dome Hon Thom Boutique Hotel, Star Bay Boutique Hotel - Fireworks Ocean View - Sunset Town Seaview - New Opening October 2026, and Lagoon Residences Phu Quoc.\n\nHow do I find a hotel in central Phu Quoc?\nAfter you launch a hotel search on KAYAK, you can refine your research by neighborhood, which allows you to pick the central Phu Quoc districts. You can also do a search using the city map to choose a specific location, like Phu Quoc city center.\n\nHow can I find hotels near me?\nTake a look at our extensive hotel map to find the best hotels near you.\n\nAre there Phu Quoc hotels with free parking?\nThere are many hotels in Phu Quoc that offer both parking and free parking. Popular choices among KAYAK users include Seashells Phu Quoc Hotel & Spa, Best Western Premier Sonasea Phu Quoc and Vinholidays Fiesta Phu Quoc.',NULL,0,'https://www.kayak.com/Phu-Quoc-Hotels.54054.hotel.ksp','Nguồn: KAYAK','2026-11-17 10:43:14','2026-11-17 11:28:32'),(5,NULL,2,'Mexico City','mexico-city','Mexico City, Mexico','kayak_82dff9a7ad6e9b0d713148deaf1dd431.jpg','Where to stay in Mexico City?\nKAYAK users usually search for hotels in Roma Norte, La Condesa and adjacent to Zona Rosa.\n\nWhat are the best hotels near Zona Rosa?\nIf you are looking for a hotel close to Zona Rosa, you should consider staying at Sofitel Mexico City Reforma, Sheraton Mexico City Maria Isabel Hotel and NH Collection Mexico City Reforma, as they are the most recommended by KAYAK users.\n\nWhat are the best hotels in Mexico City near the Polanco area?\nThe Polanco neighborhood is an upscale area that is perfect for individuals who would like to go shopping and experience a bit of luxury. The Las Alcobas is a luxury 5-star hotel that is located directly in Polanco and is only a 10-minute walk from the closest metro station. The Hyatt Regency is a slightly more affordable choice that has several onsite dining options.\n\nWhat are the best hotels in Mexico City near the Basilica of Our Lady of Guadalupe?\nThe Hotel Brasilia is a budget hotel that is near the Zócalo and the famous Basilica of Our Lady of Guadalupe. The City Express is a 4-star hotel that is also near the Basilica and only 10 minutes from the closest metro station. The Hotel Panorama offers free parking for guests and has whirlpool tubs.\n\nWhat are the best hotels in Mexico City with breakfast included?\nThe Hampton Inn & Suites Mexico City - Centro Historico is located in a beautiful, historic building and provides free hot breakfasts for guests. The Condesa Haus also comes with breakfast included and has a rooftop terrace that guests can access. The Chaya B & B Boutique is a trendy bed-and-breakfast just four minutes away from the Hidalgo metro station.\n\nWhat are the best hotels in Mexico City in the Historic District?\nThe Historico Central is located directly in the Historic District and is set in an 18th-century building. The Hotel Templo Mayor is a cheap choice located on a pedestrian-only street and only eight minutes from the Zócalo square.\n\nWhere can guests who want to experience different food scenes in Mexico City stay?\nMexico City is home to several cuisines. As a result, if you are in town and intend on sampling different cuisines, consider booking a classic room at the Four Seasons Hotel. The hotel is located within the proximity of numerous restaurants including Pan Dulce featuring classic Mexican and French pastries, Zanaya Restaurant providing authentic flavors from Mexico\'s Pacific Coast, and Becco Restaurant bringing sophisticated Italian Cuisine.\n\nWhich Mexico City hotels are ideal for those looking for tranquility?\nThose who are looking to stay in a laid-back environment during their vacation in Mexico City are not left out. The neighborhood features various hotels offering comfort and tranquility to suit your needs. In this case, Hotel Catedral is your ideal option. The establishment features soundproof rooms shielding you from the surrounding noise. In addition, you can have access to food delivery to your room.\n\nAre there Mexico City hotels offering airport shuttle services?\nAre you having an early morning flight or landing at Mexico City? Consider spending the night at the Grand Fiesta Americana Chapultepec. The hotel offers airport shuttle services to and from Benito Juarez International Airport on request. Alternatively, you can opt to stay at the Historic Central offering similar services at a surcharge.\n\nWhich hotels in Mexico City are ideal for the city’s events experience?\nDo you intend on attending various events during your trip to Mexico City? In that case, you should seek accommodations at Mexico City hotels located near these events such as Fiesta Americana Viaducto AeroPuerto. Concerts at Palacio de Los Deportes or Foro Sol, à Diablos Rojos baseball game at the Alfredo Harp Hel Stadium, and car races at Autodromo Hermanos Rodriguez are some of the events you can conveniently access from this hotel.\n\nWhich freebies do KAYAK users look for when booking a hotel in Mexico City?\nKAYAK users look for a hotel in Mexico City with free breakfast. Hotels with free breakfast in Mexico City include Casa Levora, Casa Polanco Hotel Boutique, and Las Alcobas, a Luxury Collection Hotel, Mexico City.\n\nHow do I find a hotel in central Mexico City?\nAfter you launch a hotel search on KAYAK, you can refine your research by neighborhood, which allows you to pick the central Mexico City districts. You can also do a search using the city map to choose a specific location, like Mexico City city center.\n\nHow can I find hotels near me?\nTake a look at our extensive hotel map to find the best hotels near you.\n\nAre there Mexico City hotels with free parking?\nThere are many hotels in Mexico City that offer both parking and free parking. Popular choices among KAYAK users include Exe Alameda Reforma, Hotel Geneve Mexico City and Camino Real Polanco Mexico.',NULL,0,'https://www.kayak.com/Mexico-City-Hotels.53588.hotel.ksp','Nguồn: KAYAK','2026-11-17 11:42:55',NULL),(6,NULL,3,'New York','new-york','New York, United States','kayak_32ecd987173ff7749c2d72e2762bf726.jpg','Where to stay in New York?\nWe\'ve recorded a higher demand for hotels in Manhattan, Midtown, and close to Times Square.\n\nWhat are the best hotels near Times Square?\nCarnegie Hotel, Element New York Times Square West and Club Quarters, Times Square - Midtown are very popular with users who want to stay within walking distance of Times Square.\n\nHow do I find a good hotel in the Times Square area?\nThe Times Square area offers a wide range of hotels, like the Hyatt Centric Times Square New York, which is a 4-star hotel in a great location with views of Times Square and Rockefeller Center. Similarly, The Millennium Premier New York Times Square, which is only a three-minute walk to Times Square, is a luxury hotel with good service and comprehensive amenities.\n\nWhat hotels in New York City have the best views?\nOne of New York’s most impressive features is its remarkable skyline. Views are abundant and can be found in a number of hotels, though 5-star establishments are almost always guaranteed to offer the most spectacular. If you are looking for large windows framing the Empire State Building, opt for The Bowery Hotel. The New York Edition, housed in the historic Metropolitan Life clock tower, is another great option, as are the Four Seasons and Langham Place hotels.\n\nWhat hotels in New York City have a pool?\nHotels in New York with a pool are numerous and scattered about the city, with options including the Sixty LES hotel, which offers an outdoor pool with a solarium; The Peninsula New York, if you prefer an indoor pool and spa; and Sonder The William for an outdoor pool with views of the city skyline and a perfect view of the Empire State Building.\n\nWhat are good hotels for families in New York City?\nMany NYC hotels are kid-friendly. Whether you have a large or small family, you’ll find plenty of comfort and convenience in the following establishments: The Benjamin Royal Sonesta New York, which can provide a cradle and nannies for those who need them, or the Casablanca Hotel by Library Hotel Collection , which also offers a babysitting service, family rooms, and entertainment for children, like books, puzzles and CDs.\n\nWhich hotels in New York are best for guests traveling with family?\nIf you’re traveling to New York with family, consider staying at the New Yorker Hotel or the Pod Times Square. The Pod Times Square has bunk beds available in some rooms, as well as apartments with separate living rooms, while the New Yorker provides 1-bedroom suites with sofa beds to accommodate larger families.\n\nWhere is the best place to stay in New York when I\'m traveling for business?\nIf you’re traveling to New York on business, book your stay at either the InterContinental New York Times Square or the Belvedere Hotel. Both hotels have well-supplied business centers and meeting rooms available to guests upon request.\n\nWhich hotels in New York offer accessibility services?\nWhen visiting New York, if you\'ll need special accessibility features, think about staying at the Hotel Edison or the Intercontinental New York Times Square. Both hotels have a variety of accessible amenities, such as handicap parking, an accessible pool, an elevator, and accessible bathrooms both in guest rooms and in the hotels’ common spaces. The hotels also have staff available to assist guests at any time.\n\nWhere should I stay in New York when I’m traveling with pets?\nConsider staying at the New Yorker by Wyndham or the MOXY NYC Times Square hotel if you\'re traveling to Miami with a four-legged companion. While Moxy NYC Times Square has an animal weight restriction of 25 lbs., the New Yorker enables guests to bring up to two dogs that weigh up to 45 lbs. Make sure to pass by the check-in desk at the Moxy NYC Times Square, where you can get treats for your pets.\n\nHow do I find a hotel in central New York?\nAfter you launch a hotel search on KAYAK, you can refine your research by neighborhood, which allows you to pick the central New York districts. You can also do a search using the city map to choose a specific location, like New York city center.\n\nHow can I find hotels near me?\nTake a look at our extensive hotel map to find the best hotels near you.',NULL,0,'https://www.kayak.com/New-York-Hotels.15830.hotel.ksp','Nguồn: KAYAK','2026-11-17 11:45:46','2026-11-17 11:50:36'),(7,NULL,1,'Hanoi','hanoi','Hanoi, Vietnam','kayak_dc81db9dd0b9e135cbecec64ab814ade.jpg','Where to stay in Hanoi?\nHotels adjacent to Hanoi Old Quarter and in Cau Giay or Hai Ba Trung are usually very popular with KAYAK users.\n\nWhat are the best hotels near Hanoi Old Quarter?\nIf you are looking for a hotel close to Hanoi Old Quarter, you should consider staying at Acoustic Hotel & Spa, May De Ville Lakeside Hotel and The Oriental Jade Hotel, as they are the most recommended by KAYAK users.\n\nWhich hotels in Hanoi have a good pool?\nThe Ann Hanoi Hotel is an elegant option which is only a 3-minute walk from the Red River and has a rooftop pool that provides guests with stunning views of the city. The Hanoi Club Hotel & Lake Palais Residences is located on the banks of West Lake and has an outdoor pool with an adjacent bar.\n\nWhich hotels in Hanoi are good for business travellers?\nThe Lakeside Palace Hotel is a casual choice that is a 5-minute walk from the city’s Old Quarter and has an on-site business centre. The Hilton Garden Inn is a 10-minute walk from the Hanoi Opera House and has a business centre that has several private meeting rooms.\n\nWhat are good hotels in Hanoi near the Ho Chi Minh Museum?\nThe Hanoi Delight Hotel is a straightforward choice that is located in the centre of the Ba Đình district and is a 7-minute walk away from the Ho Chi Minh Museum. The TU House Hanoi is across the street from the museum and is only a 4-minute walk from the local botanical garden.\n\nWhat are good hotels in Hanoi near the One Pillar Pagoda Buddhist temple?\nThe Hung Vuong Hotel is a laid-back hotel that is within a 5-minute walking distance to the One Pillar Pagoda and a 10-minute walk from the Ho Chi Minh Mausoleum. The Rising Dragon Villa Hotel is located in the Old Quarter and is a 9-minute walk away from the One Pillar Pagoda.\n\nWhich freebies do KAYAK users look for when booking a hotel in Hanoi?\nKAYAK users look for a hotel in Hanoi with free breakfast. Hotels with free breakfast in Hanoi include Hanoian Central Hotel & Spa, L\'Signature Hotel & Spa, and Capella Hanoi.\n\nHow do I find a hotel in central Hanoi?\nAfter you launch a hotel search on KAYAK, you can refine your research by neighborhood, which allows you to pick the central Hanoi districts. You can also do a search using the city map to choose a specific location, like Hanoi city center.\n\nHow can I find hotels near me?\nTake a look at our extensive hotel map to find the best hotels near you.\n\nAre there Hanoi hotels with free parking?\nThere are many hotels in Hanoi that offer both parking and free parking. Popular choices among KAYAK users include L7 West Lake Hanoi By Lotte, Grand Plaza Hotel Hanoi and Lotte Hotel Hanoi.',NULL,0,'https://www.kayak.com/Hanoi-Hotels.34211.hotel.ksp','Nguồn: KAYAK','2026-11-17 11:45:50','2026-11-17 11:47:53'),(8,NULL,1,'Da Nang','da-nang','Da Nang, Vietnam','kayak_a4081052b7674b884c4a40ee24b03aa1.jpg','Where to stay in Da Nang?\nHai Chau is the most popular neighborhood on KAYAK for users looking for a hotel in Da Nang. You should also consider staying close to My Khê Beach.\n\nWhat are the best hotels near My Khê Beach?\nIf you are looking for a hotel close to My Khê Beach, you should consider staying at Sala Danang Beach Hotel, Parosand Danang Hotel and Grand Tourane Hotel, as they are the most recommended by KAYAK users.\n\nWhich hotels in Da Nang are close to attractions?\nDa Nang has many delights for the casual or active sightseer. Spend the day hiking the five peaks of the Marble Mountains, then get a good night’s sleep at the Hyatt Regency Danang Resort & Spa which is located less than 0.5 km from the range. Alternatively, Sen Boutique Hotel in the city centre allows you to take in the Cham museum as well as the Dragon Bridge.\n\nWhich hotels in Da Nang are close to shopping areas?\nTravellers can stay at the Bamboo Green Riverside Hotel in Hai Chau district and visit Da Nang Souvenirs & Café with its authentic local merchandise as well as the Lotte Mart Da Nang shopping mall, which includes a supermarket. The Risemount Resort Danang located in the Ngu Hanh district puts you within easy reach of Non Nuoc Fine Arts Village and its 500 workshops and retail outlets that offer various arts, craft and jewellery.\n\nWhich hotels in Da Nang come with kitchen facilities?\nIf you wish to try your hand at preparing authentic Vietnamese cuisine, the Zen Diamond Suites Hotel near Han River Bridge has various units equipped with full kitchen facilities, stovetop and dining areas. Meanwhile, The Salamander Hotel and Apartment near My Khe Beach offers full cookware utilities as well as a microwave.\n\nWhich hotels in Da Nang are good for family vacations?\nBrilliant Hotel, just a few metres from Da Nang Cathedral, offers family friendly accommodations including free airport transfer upon request and free infant beds. Also, one child 5 years or younger can stay for free when sleeping in the same room as the parents or guardian. Holiday Beach Danang Hotel and Resort is a minute’s walk from My Khe Beach and features a free children’s area, children’s pool and on-site playground.\n\nWhich freebies do KAYAK users look for when booking a hotel in Da Nang?\nKAYAK users look for a hotel in Da Nang with free breakfast. Hotels with free breakfast in Da Nang include Monarque Hotel, Parosand Danang Hotel, and Salmalia Boutique Hotel & Spa.\n\nHow do I find a hotel in central Da Nang?\nAfter you launch a hotel search on KAYAK, you can refine your research by neighborhood, which allows you to pick the central Da Nang districts. You can also do a search using the city map to choose a specific location, like Da Nang city center.\n\nHow can I find hotels near me?\nTake a look at our extensive hotel map to find the best hotels near you.\n\nAre there Da Nang hotels with free parking?\nThere are many hotels in Da Nang that offer both parking and free parking. Popular choices among KAYAK users include Four Points by Sheraton Danang, Haian Beach Hotel & Spa and Sala Danang Beach Hotel.',NULL,0,'https://www.kayak.com/Da-Nang-Hotels.42700.hotel.ksp','Nguồn: KAYAK','2026-11-17 11:50:38',NULL),(10,NULL,4,'Singapore','singapore','Singapore, Singapore','kayak_91e4564928db7fce69949d1be8b05f1c.jpg','Where to stay in Singapore?\nHotels adjacent to Marina Bay Sands and in Kallang or Orchard are usually very popular with KAYAK users.\n\nWhat are the best hotels near Marina Bay Sands?\nKAYAK users like staying at Marina Bay Sands, The Fullerton Hotel Singapore and The Ritz-Carlton Millenia Singapore when looking for a hotel in close proximity to Marina Bay Sands.\n\nWhere is a good area to stay for the best shopping in Singapore?\nThe best shopping in Singapore can be found on Orchard Road. This bustling boulevard is overflowing with shops peddling everything from souvenirs to designer labels. Additionally, there are several malls which are connected underground. Consider staying at the Royal Plaza on Scotts or The St. Regis Singapore, both within walking distance to Orchard Road.\n\nAre there any hotels in Singapore with an infinity pool?\nThere are several hotels in Singapore that have an infinity pool. For breathtaking views of the bay, think about staying at The Westin Singapore. Another nice option is the Fullerton Hotel Singapore, which offers views of the city from its rooftop pool.\n\nWhat hotels in Singapore are located near the airport?\nThere are a number of hotels near or directly inside Singapore Changi Airport. If you\'re looking for something convenient and luxurious, try the Crowne Plaza Changi Airport. This hotel has an outdoor pool as well as spa amenities, and is located near Terminal 3.\n\nAre there any hotels in Singapore near the cruise terminal?\nThere are several hotels near the Marina Bay Cruise Center. Check out Sofitel Singapore City or Oasia Hotel Downtown, Singapore by Far East Hospitality, which features a rooftop infinity pool. Both hotels are situated directly in the city center, about one mile from the Marina Bay Cruise Center, or a 20-minute bus ride.\n\nWhat are some affordable hotels in Singapore?\nA wide range of hotels at various price points can be found throughout the city of Singapore. Guests seeking a budget-friendly option could consider Sandpiper Hotel, which is located in the vibrant neighborhood of Little India. Another great option is the top-rated budget hotel Hangout @ Mt.Emily.\n\nWhich freebies do KAYAK users look for when booking a hotel in Singapore?\nKAYAK users look for a hotel in Singapore with free breakfast. Hotels with free breakfast in Singapore include Varel Singapore, a Tribute Portfolio Hotel, Raffles Singapore, and Marina Bay Sands.\n\nHow do I find a hotel in central Singapore?\nAfter you launch a hotel search on KAYAK, you can refine your research by neighborhood, which allows you to pick the central Singapore districts. You can also do a search using the city map to choose a specific location, like Singapore city center.\n\nHow can I find hotels near me?\nTake a look at our extensive hotel map to find the best hotels near you.\n\nAre there Singapore hotels with free parking?\nThere are many hotels in Singapore that offer both parking and free parking. Popular choices among KAYAK users include Carlton Hotel Singapore, WorldHotels Elite, Royal Plaza On Scotts and Rendezvous Hotel Singapore by Far East Hospitality.',NULL,0,'https://www.kayak.com/Singapore-Hotels.20828.hotel.ksp','Nguồn: KAYAK','2026-11-18 10:33:36',NULL),(11,NULL,5,'Marrakech','marrakech','Marrakech, Morocco','kayak_78c8e9a4c02510d68d64ed0f9c73905f.jpg','Where to stay in Marrakech?\nKAYAK users usually s