Town, which offers amazing views of both the city centre and the surrounding mountains.\n\nIn which neighbourhoods can I see flora and fauna?\nThe neighbourhood of Claremont is located near the Kirstenbosch National Botanical Garden, which is home to over 7000 species of plants. The Andros Boutique Hotel is a smart accommodation choice in the area. Dolphins can be seen at the northern coast of Cape Town, very near the City Bowl.\n\nWhich hotels are close to museums?\nMost museums in Cape Town are located in the City Bowl. Staying at the Cape Town Hollow Boutique Hotel, which provides great amenities for a very affordable price, puts you within easy walking distance of the Iziko South African Museum, the South African Jewish Museum, and the South African National Gallery.\n\nAre there any 5-star hotels in Cape Town?\nThere are many! A good choice is The Table Bay Hotel, located in Green Point right next to the Victoria and Alfred Waterfront. The Table Bay Hotel offers a pool and hot tub, full spa services, a gym and a business centre.\n\nWhich freebies do KAYAK users look for when booking a hotel in Cape Town?\nKAYAK users look for a hotel in Cape Town with free breakfast. Hotels with free breakfast in Cape Town include The Cape Town EDITION(SM), Labotessa Luxury Boutique Hotel, and Ellerman House.\n\nHow do I find a hotel in central Cape Town?\nAfter you launch a hotel search on KAYAK, you can refine your research by neighborhood, which allows you to pick the central Cape Town districts. You can also do a search using the city map to choose a specific location, like Cape Town city center.\n\nHow can I find hotels near me?\nTake a look at our extensive hotel map to find the best hotels near you.\n\nAre there Cape Town hotels with free parking?\nThere are many hotels in Cape Town that offer both parking and free parking. Popular choices among KAYAK users include Hotel Verde Cape Town Airport, Lagoon Beach Hotel & Spa and Signal Hill Lodge.',NULL,1,'https://www.kayak.c