ers enjoy staying close by. Exe Hotel Colón, Claridge Hotel and Gran Hotel Argentino are recommended hotels on KAYAK within walking distance.\n\nWhat hotels in Buenos Aires offer shuttle service?\nLike most large cities, Buenos Aires has a well-developed subway system. You can take the metro all around the city from downtown to outlying suburbs. For convenience, a few local hotels however provide shuttle service such as the InterContinental Hotel, Posada de las Aguilas or Aeroparque Inn & Suites.\n\nWhere should you stay in Buenos Aires?\nAlong with downtown, you’ll enjoy staying in the Wader Puerto Madero neighborhood. A modern, waterfront community, it features green spaces, bike trails and two ship-naval museums. In the area there is the Hilton, Hotel Maderos and Anselmo Buenos Aires. Somewhat upscale, this community is also within walking distance of a number of restaurants, bars and chic boutiques.\n\nWhat hotels in Buenos Aires have their own restaurant?\nGrilled meats like short ribs, chorizo and flank are a popular dish in Buenos Aires. Other traditional foods like milianesa and locro are also a must-try for tourists. Stay at a hotel with fine dining and you’ll have a chance to sample a variety of Argentinian delicacies. Among the hotels with their own restaurant are Pestana Buenos Aires, Melia Recoleta Plaza, Fiero Hotel and Own Grand Palermo Soho.\n\nWhat hotels are close to Ezeiza Airport?\nEzeiza Airport offers most international flights to and from Buenos Aires. It has hubs for American, Delta, Air Canada and British Airways airlines. If you have a late or early flight, you might want to stay at a hotel near the airport such as EZE Inn Hotel, Hotel Plaza Central and the Holiday Inn EZE Airport.\n\nWhich freebies do KAYAK users look for when booking a hotel in Buenos Aires?\nKAYAK users look for a hotel in Buenos Aires with free breakfast. Hotels with free breakfast in Buenos Aires include Ilum Experience Home, Carles Hotel Buenos Aires, and Hub Porteño.\n\nHow do I find a hotel in central Buenos Aires?\nAfter you launch a hotel search on KAYAK, you can refine your research by neighborhood, which allows you to pick the central Buenos Aires districts. You can also do a search using the city map to choose a specific location, like Buenos Aires city center.\n\nHow can I find hotels near me?\nTake a look at our extensive hotel map to find the best hotels near you.',NULL,0,'https://www.kayak.com/Buenos-Aires-Hotels.19264.hotel.ksp','Nguồn: KAYAK','2026-11-19 16:45:50','2026-11-19 16:45:52'),(24,NULL,18,'Sydney','sydney','Sydney, Australia','kayak_dec42a4b8bf51dd9b1e11dcdcf685c2b.jpg','Where to stay in Sydney?\nThe most popular neighborhoods amongst KAYAK users are Sydney CBD and Darlinghurst. Hotels in walking-distance from Darling Harbour are also very sought-after.\n\nWhat are the best hotels near Darling Harbour?\nGreat Southern Hotel Sydney, Hilton Sydney and The Grace Hotel are very popular with users who want to stay within walking distance of Darling Harbour.\n\nWhat hotels in Sydney have a good view?\nIf you’re after panoramic views of Darling Harbour, try the Four Seasons Hotel Sydney, which is a 5-star option that overlooks the Sydney Harbour Bridge and the Sydney Opera House. Another choice is Pier One Sydney Harbour, Autograph Collection, which is right below the Harbour Bridge, and also has water and city views.\n\nWhat are good spa hotels in Sydney?\nIf you’re after boutique hotels with luxury spa treatments, then the Shangri-La Hotel, Sydney is an excellent option. It has the bonus of being close to attractions like the Harbour Bridge and the Rocks area. There’s also the Swissôtel Sydney, which offers a range of luxe signature treatments.\n\nWhat are the best family-friendly hotels in Sydney?\nThe Zara Tower Apartments and Suites is one of Sydney’s apartment hotels on the edge of the Surry Hills neighborhood and offers a nice, quiet space for families traveling together, while still staying close to the city center. For those interested in staying near the zoo, try the Meriton Suites North Sydney, and enjoy harbor views from a family suite.\n\nWhat are good hotels in Sydney near the Sydney Opera House?\nIf you’re looking for cheaper accommodation near the Opera House, try the Sydney Harbour Bed & Breakfast in the Rocks neighborhood. For those willing to splurge on luxury and convenience, the Park Hyatt Sydney provides the best views of the Opera House, right across from it. There’s also the Sydney Boulevard Hotel, which is a short walk away through the city’s Royal Botanical Gardens.\n\nDo any hotels in Sydney feature a rooftop pool?\nWhen you swim it in the rooftop Infinity pool of the Sofitel Sydney Darling Harbor, you will feel like you\'re swimming above the entire city. The rooftop also features padded lounge chairs and patio seating. Other attributes of this luxurious hotel include a fitness center, a business center, room service, and valet parking.\n\nWhich Sidney hotels provide facilities for planning a large event?\nThe Rydges Sydney Airport Hotel has over 9,000 ft² of event space, as well as a conference center. Other attributes of this well-appointed hotel include a free airport shuttle scheduled times, express check-out, and a 24-hour business center. Guess can also enjoy the outside restaurant, coffee shop, and room service.\n\nCan any hotels in Sydney help me plan my entertainment and activities during my stay?\nThe accommodating staff of Citadines Connect Sydney Airport is available 24 hours a day to help you book tours and find tickets. This hotel also features banquet facilities, room service, kids’ meals, and a 24-hour front desk. Also, cribs are available.\n\nDoes Sydney have any environmentally-friendly hotels?\nSydney hotels include a number of Travel Sustainable properties, including the QT Sydney. This richly furnished and luxurious accommodation serves locally sourced and organic food, uses eco-friendly LED lighting, has double-glazed windows, and has removed unnecessary plastics such as stirrers, cups, bottles, and cutlery. The QT also offers complimentary newspapers in the lobby and a dry-cleaning service.\n\nWhich freebies do KAYAK users look for when booking a hotel in Sydney?\nKAYAK users look for a hotel in Sydney with free breakfast. Hotels with free breakfast in Sydney include Capella Sydney, Spicers Potts Point, and Roar And Snore.\n\nHow do I find a hotel in central Sydney?\nAfter you launch a hotel search on KAYAK, you can refine your research by neighborhood, which allows you to pick the central Sydney districts. You can also do a search using the city map to choose a specific location, like Sydney city center.\n\nHow can I find hotels near me?\nTake a look at our extensive hotel map to find the best hotels near you.\n\nAre there Sydney hotels with free parking?\nThere are many hotels in Sydney that offer both parking and free parking. Popular choices among KAYAK users include Holiday Inn Warwick Farm, Q Station Sydney Harbour National Park and Arena Hotel.',NULL,1,'https://www.kayak.com/Sydney-Hotels.2258.hotel.ksp','Nguồn: KAYAK','2026-11-19 16:54:53','2026-11-19 16:54:59'),(25,NULL,19,'Auckland','auckland','Auckland, New Zealand','kayak_c393db79e40c20c2784cb3fa75a62e17.jpg','Where to stay in Auckland?\nHotels adjacent to Viaduct Harbour and in Mount Roskill or Avondale are usually very popular with KAYAK users.\n\nWhat are the best hotels near Viaduct Harbour?\nViaduct Harbour being one of the most popular landmarks in Auckland, many travelers enjoy staying close by. SkyCity Hotel, The Grand by SkyCity and Horizon by SkyCity are recommended hotels on KAYAK within walking distance.\n\nAre there hotels in Auckland with a free airport shuttle?\nThe Auckland Airport Kiwi Hotel is less than a 10-minute drive from downtown Auckland and offers many free amenities, including airport shuttle service and complimentary breakfast. The Holiday Inn is a standard 4-star choice that is only a 10-minute drive from the Stardome Observatory and offers both parking and an airport shuttle service.\n\nWhich hotels in Auckland have a good view?\nThe M Social Auckland is a trendy hotel that is located in Princes Wharf and offers a selection of rooms that provide views of the city’s harbour. The Lighter Quay is a standard choice that is located in the Wynyard Quarter and also has rooms that look out onto the water.\n\nWhat are good hotels in Auckland near Albert Park?\nThe Frienz Backpackers is a budget-friendly choice that is a 2-minute walk from Albert Park and is located directly in the city centre. The Braemar on Parliament Street is a 4-star hotel that is a 3-minute walk from Albert Park and a 10-minute walk from the Britomart train station.\n\nWhat are good hotels in Auckland near the New Zealand Maritime Museum?\nThe Hilton is a 5-star hotel that is only a 4-minute walk from the museum and is located directly on the waterfront. The Sofitel Auckland is directly across from the harbour and is a 7-minute walk from the New Zealand Maritime Museum.\n\nWhich freebies do KAYAK users look for when booking a hotel in Auckland?\nKAYAK users look for a hotel in Auckland with free parking or free breakfast. Top-rated options with free free parking in Auckland include Franklin38 and Parnell Garden Suite, while popular hotels with free breakfast in Auckland include Aristotles North Shore and Holiday Inn Auckland Airport By IHG.\n\nHow do I find a hotel in central Auckland?\nAfter you launch a hotel search on KAYAK, you can refine your research by neighborhood, which allows you to pick the central Auckland districts. You can also do a search using the city map to choose a specific location, like Auckland city center.\n\nHow can I find hotels near me?\nTake a look at our extensive hotel map to find the best hotels near you.\n\nAre there Auckland hotels with free parking?\nThere are many hotels in Auckland that offer both parking and free parking. Popular choices among KAYAK users include Holiday Inn Auckland Airport By IHG, Edit Auckland Greenlane and Mount Richmond Hotel.',NULL,0,'https://www.kayak.com/Auckland-Hotels.2575.hotel.ksp','Nguồn: KAYAK','2026-11-19 17:03:22','2026-11-19 17:03:25');
